Error [jet.InvalidScreen]: `.screen("/tasks/:task", …)` registers no screen: the path's `:task` names no field of `TaskView`.
  --> Tests/UI/web_route_path_names_no_field.jet:9:56
    |
  9 | graph: fn() -> app.App Never! { app.new("Crew").screen("/tasks/:task", task_screen) }
    |                                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A screen's state is its address: each of its fields is a `:field` segment of the path or, marked `#App.Query`, goes after `?`, and every target opens the screen from that address, so the state has one screen and each field a place in the address.
 Fix: Write the path as a string literal starting with `/`, give the view one parameter besides its `app.Remote<S>` ones, a struct whose fields each derive `Encode` and `Decode`, make the view unable to fail and give a value that derives `Encode`, name each field that isn't `#App.Query` once as a `:field` segment, and register each state at one screen.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2820
